Microservices me **authentication + authorization** ko reusable banane ka common pattern hai **API Gateway + Shared Security Library + Token based auth (JWT/OAuth2)**.  
Goal: har microservice me duplicate code na likhna.

Below practical approaches (Java/Spring ecosystem).

---

**1️⃣ API Gateway based Authentication (Recommended)**

Architecture:

```
Client
  |
  v
API Gateway (Auth filter / JWT validation)
  |
  +----> user-service
  |
  +----> order-service
  |
  +----> payment-service
```

Example using **Spring Cloud Gateway**

```java
@Component
public class JwtAuthFilter implements GlobalFilter {

    @Override
    public Mono<Void> filter(ServerWebExchange exchange, GatewayFilterChain chain) {

        String token = exchange.getRequest()
                .getHeaders()
                .getFirst(HttpHeaders.AUTHORIZATION);

        if (token == null || !token.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
            exchange.getResponse().setStatusCode(HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED);
            return exchange.getResponse().setComplete();
        }

        String jwt = token.substring(7);

        if (!JwtUtil.validate(jwt)) {
            exchange.getResponse().setStatusCode(HttpStatus.UNAUTHORIZED);
            return exchange.getResponse().setComplete();
        }

        return chain.filter(exchange);
    }
}
```

JWT utility

```java
public class JwtUtil {

    private static final String SECRET = "mysecret";

    public static boolean validate(String token) {
        try {
            Jwts.parser()
                .setSigningKey(SECRET)
                .parseClaimsJws(token);
            return true;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return false;
        }
    }

    public static Claims getClaims(String token) {
        return Jwts.parser()
                .setSigningKey(SECRET)
                .parseClaimsJws(token)
                .getBody();
    }
}
```

---

**2️⃣ Shared Security Library (Avoid duplication)**

Create common dependency.

```
security-common
   ├── JwtUtil
   ├── AuthFilter
   ├── SecurityConfig
```

Add dependency in all services.

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.company</groupId>
    <artifactId>security-common</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

Security config:

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {

        http.csrf().disable()
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/public/**").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            .addFilterBefore(new JwtFilter(), UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class);

        return http.build();
    }
}
```

---

**3️⃣ Authorization using Roles / Claims**

JWT payload example

```json
{
  "sub": "123",
  "username": "prem",
  "roles": ["ADMIN","USER"]
}
```

Authorization in controller:

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/orders")
public class OrderController {

    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
    @GetMapping("/all")
    public List<Order> getAllOrders() {
        return service.getAll();
    }

}
```

Enable method security

```java
@EnableMethodSecurity
@Configuration
public class MethodSecurityConfig {
}
```

---

**4️⃣ External Identity Provider (Enterprise Standard)**

Instead of coding auth yourself:

Use

- **Keycloak**
- **Auth0**
- **AWS Cognito**
- **Okta**

Flow:

```
Client → Keycloak (login)
Client → receives JWT
Client → API Gateway
Gateway → microservices
```

Spring config:

```yaml
spring:
  security:
    oauth2:
      resourceserver:
        jwt:
          issuer-uri: http://keycloak:8080/realms/demo
```

---

**5️⃣ Best Industry Architecture**

```
                +----------------+
Client -------->| API Gateway    |
                | JWT validation |
                +--------+-------+
                         |
             +-----------+------------+
             |                        |
     +-------v-------+        +------v-------+
     | Order Service |        | User Service |
     +---------------+        +--------------+
             |
     Shared Security Library
```

---

**6️⃣ Quick Best Practices**

- Use **JWT (stateless auth)**
- Put **authentication in API Gateway**
- Use **shared security dependency**
- Use **Keycloak / OAuth2 for enterprise**
- Put **authorization via roles/claims**

