## 🎯 **Short Interview Answer**

> Factory Method creates a single object and allows subclasses to decide which class to instantiate, whereas Abstract Factory creates families of related objects without specifying their concrete classes. Factory Method focuses on one product, while Abstract Factory focuses on groups of related products.

A **pattern** and an **anti-pattern** both describe recurring approaches in software design, but they represent **opposite outcomes**.

