## `@FunctionalInterface` Annotation (Java 8)

👉 **Definition (crisp)**  
`@FunctionalInterface` ensures that an interface has **exactly one abstract method**.

---

## Basic Example
```java id="z0c9c4"
@FunctionalInterface
interface MyFunc {
    void apply();
}
```

---

## Compile-Time Safety ✅

```java id="p5u1qk"
@FunctionalInterface
interface Test {
    void a();
    void b(); // ❌ Compile-time error
}
```

👉 Compiler error because more than 1 abstract method

---

## Valid with Default & Static Methods
```java id="6a6o4n"
@FunctionalInterface
interface Demo {
    void run();

    default void log() {
        System.out.println("log");
    }

    static void util() {
        System.out.println("util");
    }
}
```

---

## Without Annotation (Still Works)
```java id="3d6y9k"
