Here are **industry-level implementations** of **Retry Logic with Exponential Backoff (Java)** 👇

---

### 1. Basic Retry with Exponential Backoff 🔥
```java id="rb1"
public class Retry {

    public static <T> T retry(Callable<T> task,
                              int maxAttempts,
                              long initialDelayMs) throws Exception {

        int attempt = 0;
        long delay = initialDelayMs;

        while (true) {
            try {
                return task.call();
            } catch (Exception e) {
                attempt++;

                if (attempt >= maxAttempts) {
                    throw e;
                }

                Thread.sleep(delay);
                delay *= 2; // exponential backoff
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Retry with Jitter (Best Practice 🔥🔥🔥)
```java id="rb2"
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ThreadLocalRandom;

public class Retry {

    public static <T> T retry(Callable<T> task,
                              int maxAttempts,
                              long baseDelay) throws Exception {

        int attempt = 0;

        while (true) {
            try {
                return task.call();
            } catch (Exception e) {
                attempt++;

                if (attempt >= maxAttempts) throw e;

                long jitter = ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextLong(baseDelay);
                long delay = (long) Math.pow(2, attempt) * baseDelay + jitter;

                Thread.sleep(delay);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

