### 4. Leading + Trailing Debounce 🔥
```java id="deb4"
import java.util.concurrent.*;

class Debouncer {
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler =
            Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();

    private ScheduledFuture<?> future;
    private boolean leadingCalled = false;

    public void debounce(Runnable task, long delayMs, boolean leading) {

        if (leading && !leadingCalled) {
            task.run();
            leadingCalled = true;
        }

        if (future != null && !future.isDone()) {
            future.cancel(false);
        }

        future = scheduler.schedule(() -> {
            if (!leading) task.run();
            leadingCalled = false;
        }, delayMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }
}
```

---

### 5. Debounce with Return Value (Future 🔥)
```java id="deb5"
import java.util.concurrent.*;

class Debouncer {
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler =
            Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();

    private ScheduledFuture<?> future;

    public <T> Future<T> debounce(Callable<T> task, long delayMs) {
        if (future != null && !future.isDone()) {
            future.cancel(false);
        }

        return (Future<T>) scheduler.schedule(task, delayMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }
}
```

