Here are **industry-level ways** to **remove Nth node from end of linked list** 👇

---

### 1. Two Pointer (Most Important 🔥 O(n), O(1))
```java id="rm1"
public class RemoveNth {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node next;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static Node removeNthFromEnd(Node head, int n) {
        Node dummy = new Node(0);
        dummy.next = head;

        Node fast = dummy, slow = dummy;

        // move fast n+1 steps
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            fast = fast.next;
        }

        while (fast != null) {
            fast = fast.next;
            slow = slow.next;
        }

        // remove node
        slow.next = slow.next.next;

        return dummy.next;
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Using Length Count
```java id="rm2"
static Node removeNthFromEnd(Node head, int n) {
    int size = 0;
    Node curr = head;

    while (curr != null) {
        size++;
        curr = curr.next;
    }

    if (n == size) return head.next;

    curr = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < size - n; i++) {
        curr = curr.next;
    }

    curr.next = curr.next.next;
    return head;
}
```

