Here are **industry-level ways** to **validate if a binary tree is a BST** 👇

---

### 1. Min-Max Range (Most Important 🔥 O(n))
```java id="vbst1"
public class ValidateBST {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node left, right;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static boolean isValidBST(Node root) {
        return validate(root, Long.MIN_VALUE, Long.MAX_VALUE);
    }

    static boolean validate(Node node, long min, long max) {
        if (node == null) return true;

        if (node.val <= min || node.val >= max) return false;

        return validate(node.left, min, node.val) &&
               validate(node.right, node.val, max);
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Inorder Traversal (Sorted Check 🔥)
```java id="vbst2"
static Integer prev = null;

static boolean isValidBST(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return true;

    if (!isValidBST(root.left)) return false;

    if (prev != null && root.val <= prev) return false;
    prev = root.val;

    return isValidBST(root.right);
}
```

---

### 3. Iterative Inorder 🔥🔥
```java id="vbst3"
import java.util.*;

static boolean isValidBST(Node root) {
    Stack<Node> stack = new Stack<>();
    Node curr = root;
    Integer prev = null;

    while (curr != null || !stack.isEmpty()) {
        while (curr != null) {
            stack.push(curr);
            curr = curr.left;
        }

        curr = stack.pop();

        if (prev != null && curr.val <= prev) return false;
        prev = curr.val;

        curr = curr.right;
    }

    return true;
}
```

