### 4. Using Pair (Return Range 🔥)
```java id="vbst4"
class Pair {
    boolean isBST;
    int min, max;

    Pair(boolean b, int mi, int ma) {
        isBST = b;
        min = mi;
        max = ma;
    }
}

static Pair check(Node root) {
    if (root == null)
        return new Pair(true, Integer.MAX_VALUE, Integer.MIN_VALUE);

    Pair left = check(root.left);
    Pair right = check(root.right);

    boolean isBST = left.isBST && right.isBST &&
                    root.val > left.max &&
                    root.val < right.min;

    int min = Math.min(root.val, left.min);
    int max = Math.max(root.val, right.max);

    return new Pair(isBST, min, max);
}
```

