Here are **industry-level ways** to find the **diameter of a binary tree** 👇

---

### 1. Optimized DFS (Most Important 🔥 O(n))
```java id="dia1"
public class DiameterTree {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node left, right;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static int diameter = 0;

    static int height(Node root) {
        if (root == null) return 0;

        int left = height(root.left);
        int right = height(root.right);

        diameter = Math.max(diameter, left + right);

        return 1 + Math.max(left, right);
    }

    static int diameterOfTree(Node root) {
        height(root);
        return diameter;
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Return Height + Diameter Together 🔥
```java id="dia2"
class Pair {
    int height, diameter;

    Pair(int h, int d) {
        height = h;
        diameter = d;
    }
}

static Pair solve(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return new Pair(0, 0);

    Pair left = solve(root.left);
    Pair right = solve(root.right);

    int height = 1 + Math.max(left.height, right.height);

    int diaThroughRoot = left.height + right.height;
    int diameter = Math.max(diaThroughRoot,
                     Math.max(left.diameter, right.diameter));

    return new Pair(height, diameter);
}
```

