Here are **industry-level implementations** of a **Distributed Unique ID Generator (Snowflake style)** 👇

---

### 1. Snowflake Generator (64-bit ID 🔥🔥🔥)
```java id="sf1"
public class Snowflake {

    private final long epoch = 1609459200000L; // custom epoch (2021)

    private final long nodeIdBits = 10;
    private final long sequenceBits = 12;

    private final long maxNodeId = (1L << nodeIdBits) - 1;
    private final long maxSequence = (1L << sequenceBits) - 1;

    private final long nodeId;
    private long sequence = 0L;
    private long lastTimestamp = -1L;

    private final long nodeShift = sequenceBits;
    private final long timeShift = sequenceBits + nodeIdBits;

    public Snowflake(long nodeId) {
        if (nodeId < 0 || nodeId > maxNodeId) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid nodeId");
        }
        this.nodeId = nodeId;
    }

    public synchronized long nextId() {
        long timestamp = currentTime();

        if (timestamp < lastTimestamp) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Clock moved backwards");
        }

        if (timestamp == lastTimestamp) {
            sequence = (sequence + 1) & maxSequence;

            if (sequence == 0) {
                timestamp = waitNextMillis(lastTimestamp);
            }
        } else {
            sequence = 0;
        }

        lastTimestamp = timestamp;

        return ((timestamp - epoch) << timeShift)
                | (nodeId << nodeShift)
                | sequence;
    }

    private long waitNextMillis(long lastTs) {
        long ts = currentTime();
        while (ts <= lastTs) {
            ts = currentTime();
        }
        return ts;
    }

    private long currentTime() {
        return System.currentTimeMillis();
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Thread-Safe (High Concurrency 🔥)
```java id="sf2"
import java.util.concurrent.locks.*;

public class Snowflake {

    private final Lock lock = new ReentrantLock();

    private long lastTimestamp = -1;
    private long sequence = 0;

    public long nextId() {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            return generate();
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    private long generate() {
        long ts = System.currentTimeMillis();

        if (ts == lastTimestamp) {
            sequence = (sequence + 1) & 4095;
        } else {
            sequence = 0;
        }

        lastTimestamp = ts;

        return (ts << 22) | sequence;
    }
}
```

---

### 3. Using Atomic (Lock-Free 🔥)
```java id="sf3"
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;

class Snowflake {

    private AtomicLong lastTs = new AtomicLong(-1);
    private AtomicLong seq = new AtomicLong(0);

    public long nextId() {
        long ts = System.currentTimeMillis();

        if (ts == lastTs.get()) {
            seq.set((seq.get() + 1) & 4095);
        } else {
            seq.set(0);
            lastTs.set(ts);
        }

        return (ts << 22) | seq.get();
    }
}
```

