**Purpose of `setAccessible(true)` (code-first 👇)**

👉 It **disables Java access checks** so you can access **private / protected / default members** via Reflection.

---

## 🔹 Without `setAccessible(true)` ❌

```java id="a11"
class User {
    private String name = "Prem";
}

User u = new User();

Field f = User.class.getDeclaredField("name");
// f.setAccessible(true); // not set

System.out.println(f.get(u)); // ❌ IllegalAccessException
```

---

## 🔹 With `setAccessible(true)` ✅

```java id="a12"
Field f = User.class.getDeclaredField("name");
f.setAccessible(true); // bypass access check

User u = new User();
System.out.println(f.get(u)); // ✅ Prem
```

