### ✅ 1. Avoid `System.out.println` → Use Logger
```java
package com.prem.kafka.demo;

import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.kafka.annotation.KafkaListener;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Slf4j
@Service
public class KafkaConsumerService {

    @KafkaListener(topics = "test", groupId = "test-group")
    public void consume(String message) {
        log.info("Consumed: {}", message);

        try {
            process(message);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Error processing message: {}", message, e);
            throw e; // important for retry/DLT
        }
    }

    private void process(String message) throws InterruptedException {
        log.info("Processing message...");
        Thread.sleep(3000);
        log.info("Finished processing: {}", message);
    }
}
```

---

### ✅ 2. Don’t Block Consumer Thread (VERY IMPORTANT 🚨)

❌ `Thread.sleep()` → blocks Kafka thread  
✅ Use async processing

```java
@KafkaListener(topics = "test", groupId = "test-group")
public void consume(String message) {
    CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
        try {
            process(message);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Async error", e);
        }
    });
}
```

---

### ✅ 3. Manual Acknowledgement (Better Control)

```java
import org.springframework.kafka.support.Acknowledgment;

@KafkaListener(topics = "test", groupId = "test-group")
public void consume(String message, Acknowledgment ack) {
    try {
        process(message);
        ack.acknowledge(); // commit only after success
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("Processing failed", e);
        // no ack → retry possible
    }
}
```

👉 config:
```properties
spring.kafka.listener.ack-mode=manual
```

---

### ✅ 4. Concurrency (Parallel Consumers 🚀)

```java
@KafkaListener(
    topics = "test",
    groupId = "test-group",
    concurrency = "3"
)
public void consume(String message) {
    process(message);
}
```

---

### ✅ 5. Use DTO instead of String (Real-world use)

```java
@Data
public class TodoEvent {
    private String id;
    private String title;
    private String action;
}
```

```java
