## 🔹 SAGA Pattern (Concept)

```text id="sg0"
SAGA = Distributed transactions ko manage karne ka pattern
→ Multiple services me transaction ko split karta hai
→ Har step ka ek "compensation" (rollback) hota hai
```

---

## 🔹 Example Flow (Order Service)

```text id="sg1"
1. Create Order  ✅
2. Reserve Inventory ✅
3. Payment Deduct ✅

❌ Agar Payment fail:
→ Inventory release
→ Order cancel
```

---

## 🔹 2 Types of SAGA

```text id="sg2"
1. Choreography → Events based (Kafka)
2. Orchestration → Central controller (Saga Orchestrator)
```

---

## 🔹 1. Choreography (Kafka आधारित)

### Order Service
```java id="sg3"
kafkaTemplate.send("order-created", order);
```

### Inventory Service
```java id="sg4"
@KafkaListener(topics = "order-created")
public void reserve(Order order) {
    // reserve inventory
    kafkaTemplate.send("inventory-reserved", order);
}
```

### Payment Service
```java id="sg5"
@KafkaListener(topics = "inventory-reserved")
public void pay(Order order) {
    if (fail) {
        kafkaTemplate.send("payment-failed", order);
    } else {
        kafkaTemplate.send("payment-success", order);
    }
}
```

### Compensation
```java id="sg6"
@KafkaListener(topics = "payment-failed")
public void rollback(Order order) {
    // release inventory + cancel order
}
```

---

## 🔹 2. Orchestration (Central Controller)

```java id="sg7"
@Service
public class SagaOrchestrator {

    public void process(Order order) {
        try {
            orderService.create(order);
            inventoryService.reserve(order);
            paymentService.pay(order);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // compensation
            inventoryService.release(order);
            orderService.cancel(order);
        }
    }
}
```

---

## 🔹 Key Points 🔥

```text id="sg8"
✔ No global transaction (no 2PC)
✔ Each service has local DB transaction
✔ Failure → compensation logic
✔ Eventual consistency
```

---

## 🔹 When to Use

```text id="sg9"
Microservices architecture me
Distributed transactions handle karne ke liye
```

---

## 🔹 Interview One-Liner 🔥
```text id="sg10"
Saga pattern breaks a distributed transaction into smaller local transactions with compensating actions to maintain eventual consistency.
```

